# What a buff shows - the affect bar's icons and their tooltips (uiaffectbar.py),
# the target board's row of them, the line that floats up when one ends - and
# the bonus lines a buff and an item share (localeinfo_point.py), the buff
# potions' groups and the Sprint's costs: the package's own keys, which the EN
# locale_game.txt never had, so an English client showed every one of them in
# Polish (Jeremus-Sama, 28 September). These have their English in the
# official data. The sixteen skill buffs are the r40250 client's own affect
# names: its EN locale_game.txt holds them under the keys this client renamed
# (SKILL_HOSIN, SKILL_KWAESOK...), whose Polish values are this client's word
# for word - so the affect bar says "Speed" and "Battle Flush" where the skill
# window says "Swiftness" and "Berserk", as that client did. The item-shop
# buffs are their items' names in the EN item_names.txt, and the rest the EN
# skilldesc.txt's line for the same Polish words.
